{"case_id":"T8016","gap_exists":true,"gap_type":["entry point","API protocol","state","configuration","input semantics"],"confidence":99,"affected_functions":["xmlSwitchEncodingName","xmlSwitchEncoding","xmlCreatePushParserCtxt","xmlParseChunk","xmlCtxtResetPush","xmlParseTryOrFinish","xmlStopParser","xmlErrMemory","xmlVErrParser","xmlParseDocument"],"reason":"H0 is only shared fuzz-data, entity-loader, file-slurping, and allocation-injection support; it contains no fuzz entry point and never drives a parser. It therefore cannot exercise the materially changed push-parser lifecycle, encoding-selection APIs, parser stop/error states, or allocation-failure propagation in S1.","evidence":["H0 defines helpers such as xmlFuzzDataInit, xmlFuzzReadEntities, xmlFuzzEntityLoader, and xmlFuzzMemSetLimit, but contains no LLVMFuzzerTestOneInput-equivalent target and no call to xmlParseDocument, xmlCreatePushParserCtxt, xmlParseChunk, xmlCtxtResetPush, xmlSwitchEncoding, or xmlSwitchEncodingName.","S1 adds the public xmlSwitchEncodingName declaration and implementation, and routes encoding names through it from xmlCtxtResetPush, xmlDoRead, xmlParseInNodeContext, xmlSetDeclaredEncoding, and xmlCheckHTTPInput.","The xmlParseChunk protocol changes materially: processing is rejected whenever disableSAX is nonzero, chunk acceptance no longer depends on instate != XML_PARSER_EOF, and oversized lookup state now reports XML_ERR_RESOURCE_LIMIT.","PARSER_STOPPED(ctxt) is introduced as disableSAX > 1, xmlHaltParser sets disableSAX = 2, ordinary fatal errors can set disableSAX = 1, and numerous parsing loops switch from XML_PARSER_EOF checks to this new state distinction.","xmlErrMemory now sets errNo to XML_ERR_NO_MEMORY, wellFormed to 0, disableSAX to 2, and dispatches error callbacks; H0 provides failure injection but has no parser invocation that can validate these state transitions."],"recommended_action":"Add a dedicated parser fuzz target that consumes fuzz bytes as both XML data and control fields, exercises one-shot and push parsing with varied chunk boundaries and terminate sequences, selects enum- and name-based encodings including unsupported names, varies parser options such as XML_PARSE_HUGE and recovery, invokes xmlStopParser during callbacks, and iterates allocation-failure points while checking cleanup and stable error/state behavior."}
